<%# One resolved care field: an uppercase label on its own line — not inline
    with its value, which is the hierarchy fix this redesign turns on — then
    the value. A picked (multi_select) set renders as one chip per value,
    tinted to the section's colour; short_text is the parent's own words and
    always prints as a sentence, never chipped.

    `chips:` is false in the half-page's middle overflow tier: same field,
    same values, comma-joined text instead of chips (roughly half the height
    per row) — see _care_plan_card.html.erb. %>
<div class="row">
  <span class="k"><%= field.label %></span>
  <% if field.type == :short_text %>
    <div class="say"><%= field.values.first %></div>
  <% elsif chips %>
    <div class="chips">
      <% field.values.each do |value| %><span class="chip"><%= value %></span><% end %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <div class="text"><%= field.values.join(", ") %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
